 "other": 423, "system": 32462, "tool_definitions": 14397, "tool_results": 60318}, "measure": "json-utf8-bytes", "total_bytes": 194255}, "gateway_set": ["thinking.display"], "web_search": false, "web_searches": 0, "calls": {"Bash": 1}}}, {"id": "ae010daa-f4b6-5d26-8648-4fe52b465d5c", "at": 1795645457.6402957, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 9498, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "story-repo", "actor": "story-repo", "execution_id": "da273c05083ed0a04ef77840c174b67e", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "usage", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "context usage"}, {"id": "146b17fa-50e3-5ba3-9101-2071c3af5dd6", "at": 1795645459.061208, "until": 1795645461.2534814, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 9499, "layer": "worker", "category": "thinking", "kind": "session.agent_thought_chunk", "role": "story-repo", "actor": null, "execution_id": "da273c05083ed0a04ef77840c174b67e", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "thinking", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "thinking (48 chunks, content withheld)"}, {"id": "61afdf48-1387-5bd0-9968-9eb9a44b17da", "at": 1795645461.256314, "until": 1795645471.3930814, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 9597, "layer": "worker", "category": "execute", "kind": "tool.pending", "role": "story-repo", "actor": "story-repo", "execution_id": "da273c05083ed0a04ef77840c174b67e", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": "completed", "label": "execute → completed", "repository": null, "tool_call_id": "toolu_01BNTRPT7xHbQRAG7Zh8Fubw", "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "cd /hutian/scratch/sw; git remote set-url origin $HT_FORGEJO_URL/world/story-repo.wiki.git; python3 - <<'EOF' p='Outline.md'; s=open(p).read() def rep(a,b): global s assert a in s, a[:50]; s=s.replace(a,b,1) rep(\"reported gap = mean over d…", "shown": {"trace": {"input": [["command", "cd /hutian/scratch/sw; git remote set-url origin $HT_FORGEJO_URL/world/story-repo.wiki.git; python3 - <<'EOF'\np='Outline.md'; s=open(p).read()\ndef rep(a,b):\n    global s\n    assert a in s, a[:50]; s=s.replace(a,b,1)\nrep(\"reported gap = mean over disjoint-S draws and rotations of (naive score on S − accuracy on the verification block), minus nothing (the verification noise is zero-mean, it widens the interval, not the bias).\",\n    \"reported gap = mean over disjoint-S draws and rotations of (naive score on S − accuracy on the verification block). The gap is not corrected for verification noise, which has zero mean and only widens the interval.\")\nrep(\"### 2.1 Pre-specified decision rules (the analysis plan; to be accepted/amended by experiment-repo)\\n\",\n\"\"\"### 2.1 Pre-specified decision rules (the analysis plan; to be accepted/amended by experiment-repo)\n**Two general rules (added after idea-review of v2).**\n(a) **Which interval each rule uses.** Draws of S overlap heavily within a rotation, so the number of draws buys precision only on the *pool-conditional* rate (binomial/MC SE over draws). Every rule below that says something about behaviour on the benchmark (\"above nominal\", \"valid\", \"detectable\", \"within\") uses the **between-pool bootstrap interval**, not the binomial one; the binomial MC SE is reported as the precision of the pool-conditional rate and is used only to size the number of draws.\n(b) **How truth enters coverage and overstatement.** On the real matrix θ(ĉ) is observed only as accuracy Â_ver on a ≈300-item verification block (noise ≈ 0.03, as large as the gap), so \"L ≤ θ(ĉ)\" is not observable. Every coverage and P(report > θ(ĉ)) number on real data is therefore reported as a **pair**: an anti-conservative score (L ≤ Â_ver; point report > Â_ver) and a conservative score (L ≤ Â_ver + z·SE_ver), and a validity statement on real data is made only when it holds for the pair as written in the rule (valid = conservative score meets the criterion; invalid = the anti-conservative score fails it; otherwise \"indeterminate at this verification noise\"). The **synthetic and semi-synthetic arms, where θ is exact,** are the primary place for coverage/overstatement thresholds; the same scoring is run there to show how far verification noise moves each criterion, and the criterion tolerances (the 0.5 ± 0.05 and 0.95 − 2·MC SE below) are restated for the real matrix from that bias before the real matrix is analysed. Analysis may propose a less noisy truth (e.g. larger verification blocks at fewer rotations) if its design allows it.\n\n\"\"\")\nrep(\"**C4:** a rate is \\\"above nominal\\\" when its 95% interval excludes nominal + 1 pp (at α=0.05), based on ≥2000 draws per cell;\",\n    \"**C4:** a rate is \\\"above nominal\\\" when its 95% **between-pool bootstrap** interval excludes nominal + 1 pp (at α=0.05); ≥2000 draws per cell give a pool-conditional MC SE ≤ 0.5 pp and nothing more;\")\nrep(\"primary validity = one-sided 95% lower-bound coverage ≥ 0.95 − 2·MC SE, in all primary cells;\",\"primary validity = one-sided 95% lower-bound coverage ≥ 0.95 − 2·SE (SE from the between-pool bootstrap on real data, from the MC SE on the synthetic arm), in all primary cells, scored as in (b);\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngit commit -qam \"Outline: intervals per rule and noisy-truth scoring (idea-review v2 points)\"; git push -q origin HEAD:main && git push -q origin HEAD:master; git log -1 --oneline\ncd /hutian/repo; forge issue comment 3 -b \"Both points taken in Outline §2.1: general rule (a) says which interval each rule uses (between-pool bootstrap; draws size pool-conditional precision only); rule (b) scores coverage/overstatement on real data as an anti-conservative/conservative pair, with exact-θ synthetic arms setting the thresholds before the real matrix is analysed. C1 wording fixed.\" | tail -1; forge issue close 3"]], "output": "```console\n7d68fb3 Outline: intervals per rule and noisy-truth scoring (idea-review v2 points)\nhttp://172.17.0.1:39161/world/story-repo/issues/3#issuecomment-33\nClosed #3\n```", "exit": null}}}, {"id": "e1784130-663e-5580-b191-227f23d22813", "at": 1795645469.7577777, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 9669, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.session/request_permission", "role": "story-repo", "actor": "story-repo", "execution_id": "da273c05083ed0a04ef77840c174b67e", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "session/request_permission"}, {"id": "3b214ca4-8477-57a4-a378-4d11f54e3a3a", "at": 1795645469.7606492, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 9670, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.response", "role": "story-repo", "actor": "story-repo", "execution_id": "da273c05083ed0a04ef77840c174b67e", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "response"}, {"id": "b8c36067-2013-5df5-b063-dd9ff431ba7a", "at": 1795645469.7640095, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 9671, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "story-repo", "actor": "story-repo", "execution_id": "da273c05083ed0a04ef77840c174b67e", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "usage", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "context usage"}, {"id": "353a8098-f74f-5732-b044-691240d1e1e0", "at": 1795645469.9137084, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 9673, "layer": "worker", "category": "challenge", "kind": "authentication.challenge", "role": "story-repo", "actor": "unknown", "execution_id": "da273c05083ed0a04ef77840c174b67e", "trust": "system-confirmed", "outcome": "credential-required", "label": "challenge → credential-required", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "credential challenge GET /world/story-repo.wiki.git/info/refs"}, {"id": "1614b58a-14a7-53f9-b89b-04bde3c6f53c", "at": 