ule”"}, {"id": "ee68aedb-0653-5346-a7e4-76371c3f382b", "at": 1795645472.761714, "clock": "world", "stream": "world", "sequence": 260, "layer": "role", "category": "obligation", "kind": "obligation.changed", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "dispatcher", "execution_id": null, "trust": "system-confirmed", "outcome": "open", "label": "changed answered:story-repo#3 v2", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [{"ref": "b1abd8ab-1b4f-5bdb-b823-a3e0a9dfd6f5", "relation": "caused-by", "trust": "system-confirmed"}], "obligation": {"key": "answered:story-repo#3", "kind": "answered", "version": 2, "change": "changed", "cause": "closed", "source": "forgejo"}, "summary": "answered:story-repo#3 “Review of Outline v2: truth noise in coverage criteria; interval used by each rule” changed → v2 (closed)"}, {"id": "1c7fb227-da7f-5411-ac0f-7ee495e566c6", "at": 1795645475.78385, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 9691, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "story-repo", "actor": "story-repo", "execution_id": "da273c05083ed0a04ef77840c174b67e", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "ambiguous_order": true, "label": "usage", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "context usage"}, {"id": "7fa8aa9f-6f88-5abc-9a13-f67cfbf2376e", "at": 1795645475.8037152, "until": 1795645476.035327, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 9692, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.agent_message_chunk", "role": "story-repo", "actor": "story-repo", "execution_id": "da273c05083ed0a04ef77840c174b67e", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "ambiguous_order": true, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "message (65 chunks)", "shown": {"message": "I took both review points from `idea-review-repo`#3 into §2.1 of the outline and pushed it. I also fixed the C1 wording and closed the issue.\n\n- **Which interval each rule uses:** every rule that makes a statement about behaviour on the benchmark now uses the between-pool bootstrap interval. The number of draws only sets the precision of the pool-conditional rate.\n- **Noisy truth:** on the real matrix, coverage and \"report overstates\" are each scored two ways. The anti-conservative score is \"bound ≤ verification accuracy\". The conservative score is \"bound ≤ verification accuracy plus z·SE\". A validity claim on real data needs the pair to agree. The synthetic and semi-synthetic arms, where the true accuracy is exact, set the thresholds. Those thresholds are restated for the real matrix before it is analysed.\n\nI'm still waiting on `experiment-repo` to accept or amend these rules in its issue #4."}}, {"id": "5cf2031a-d989-515f-8c45-5766557ab862", "at": 1795645476.2097378, "clock": "world", "stream": "world", "sequence": 261, "layer": "role", "category": "wiki", "kind": "collaboration.wiki", "role": "story-repo", "actor": "story-repo", "execution_id": "da273c05083ed0a04ef77840c174b67e", "trust": "system-confirmed", "outcome": "observed", "attributed": "inferred", "ambiguous_order": true, "label": "story-repo wiki edited story-repo", "repository": "world/story-repo", "flags": [], "causes": [{"ref": "segment:da273c05083ed0a04ef77840c174b67e", "relation": "during-turn", "trust": "inferred"}], "forgejo": {"kind": "wiki", "repository": "world/story-repo", "thread": null, "object_id": null, "action": "edited"}, "summary": "story-repo edited wiki page story-repo:“Outline”: “Outline: intervals per rule and noisy-truth scoring (idea-review v2 points)”"}, {"id": "618854d9-ce45-5e4e-ab05-c4d599045d2f", "at": 1795645476.210835, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 9758, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "story-repo", "actor": "story-repo", "execution_id": "da273c05083ed0a04ef77840c174b67e", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "ambiguous_order": true, "label": "usage", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary"